      "text": "We can start by setting up a calendar and marking each person's working days.\n\n- Darren works every 3 days, so his working days are days 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, etc.\n- Wanda works every 4 days, so her working days are days 4, 8, 12, 16, etc.\n- Beatrice works every 6 days, so her working days are days 6, 12, 18, 24, etc.\n- Chi works every 7 days, so her working days are days 7, 14, 21, 28, etc.\n\nFrom the calendar, we can see that they all work on the same day every 42 school days (the least common multiple of 3, 4, 6, and 7). Therefore, in \\boxed{42} school days from today, they will all be working in the lab together.",
