    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let $x$ be the number of school days from today that they will next be together.\nIn $x$ days, Darren will have worked $x/3$ times.\nIn $x$ days, Wanda will have worked $x/4$ times.\nIn $x$ days, Beatrice will have worked $x/6$ times.\nIn $x$ days, Chi will have worked $x/7$ times.\nThey will all be working together when these values are all equal.\nTherefore, we have the following simultaneous equations:\n$x/3 = x/4 = x/6 = x/7$\nMultiplying through by 84 to clear the denominators, we get:\n$28x = 21x = 14x = 12x$\nSolving this equation, we find that $x = 84$.\nTherefore, they will all be together tutoring in the lab in $\\boxed{84}$ school days.\nThe answer is: 84",
