    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Since they are working as tutors in the lab together today, we need to find the first instance that it will not happen in the future.\n\nTo determine this, let x represent the number of school days from today. Since Darren works every third school day, x/3 will be a multiple of Darren's working cycle. Similarly, let x/4 be a multiple of Darren's working cycle for Wanda. Let x/6 be a multiple of Betty's cycle, and similarly, x/7 is a multiple of Chi's cycle. From this information, we determine:\n\n3n1 = x – multiple of 6\n4n2 = x – multiple of 5\nx = 1 is not a multiple of 3n3 + 1\nx = 3 is not a multiple of 6n3 + 1\n1 = 2 is not a multiple of 4n3 + 1\nx = 6 is not a multiple of 5n3 + 1\nThe first instance that will not occur from today will also be the next instance that one of them will not be working is when x = 21 and Chi cannot be working as an independent process. For Δ, Wanda, 3n4 + 1, 6n1 + 1, and Chi are not matching factors. To find the number of school days from today, we identify the one when the last common multiple is not required to be accounted for yet.\n\nHence,\nx = 21\nSo, the answer is \\boxed{21}.",
