    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find out in how many school days from today Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab, we need to determine the least common multiple (LCM) of their working intervals. Darren works every 3 days, Wanda every 4 days, Beatrice every 6 days, and Chi every 7 days. Therefore, we need to find the LCM of 3, 4, 6, and 7.\n\n1. **Prime Factorization:**\n   - \\(3 = 3\\)\n   - \\(4 = 2^2\\)\n   - \\(6 = 2 \\cdot 3\\)\n   - \\(7 = 7\\)\n\n2. **Identify the highest power of each prime factor:**\n   - The highest power of 2 in the factorization is \\(2^2 = 4\\).\n   - The highest power of 3 in the factorization is \\(3^1 = 3\\).\n   - The highest power of 7 in the factorization is \\(7^1 = 7\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the LCM by multiplying these highest powers together:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{LCM} = 2^2 \\cdot 3^1 \\cdot 7^1 = 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 7\n   \\]\n\n4. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   4 \\cdot 3 = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   12 \\cdot 7 = 84\n   \\]\n\nThus, Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab after \\(\\boxed{84}\\) school days.",
